![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The PR description mentions strengthening the `listRecent` limit test with an ordering assertion (`['r3', 'r2']`), but this assertion is currently missing from the test.

```typescript
    expect(records).toHaveLength(2);
    expect(records.map(r => r.id)).toEqual(['r3', 'r2']);
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The PR description states that fault fixtures are exported as `unknown`. However, `compiledPromptFaultFixture` is currently cast to `CompiledPrompt` using `as unknown as CompiledPrompt`.

```suggestion
export const compiledPromptFaultFixture = {
  imagePrompt: '',
  negativePrompt: '',
  metadata: {
    glamLevel: 0,
    density: 'medium',
    lineThickness: 'medium',
    borderStyle: 'none',
    stylePreset: '',
    enforcedConstraints: []
  }
} as unknown;
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The header comment states that the mock uses in-memory state 'seeded from fixtures' and has an info flow to 'fixtures'. However, the mock is initialized with an empty array and does not import or use any fixtures. The header comment should be corrected to reflect this.

```suggestion
// Purpose: Mock GalleryStoreSeam behavior using in-memory state.
// Why: Keep tests deterministic without live I/O; zero invented data.
// Info flow: tests -> mock.
```
